# The difference of two balls with 2-limb centers: ball_add_2 with the second center negated.
kernel:        ball_sub_2
input:         cx = cx0 cx1
input:         rx
input:         cy = cy0 cy1
input:         ry
output:        cz = cz0 cz1
output:        rz
value:         cx-cy
requires:      normalized cx
requires:      nonneg rx
requires:      normalized cy
requires:      nonneg ry
ensures:       normalized cz
ensures:       encloses cz rz x-y x=cx,rx y=cy,ry
min_precision: 3
source:        midpoint-radius difference (Milestone 1 listing)
status:        unverified
cone_exempt:   the radius never reaches the center; the special states of the ball layer (Milestone 1 statements, Ball kernels) test the center and the radii

(n0, n1)        = neg_2(cy0, cy1)
(cz0, cz1, rz)  = ball_add_2(cx0, cx1, rx, n0, n1, ry)
